{
  "type": "doc",
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In Part 2, I installed QueryPie ACP Community Edition on my Mac and signed in. Now I want to connect a database and query test data."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "What interested me was the developer experience. Once an administrator registers a database, where does a developer run SQL? Is access limited to the browser, or can an existing database client be used?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I created a test orders database and queried it in QueryPie’s web interface. Then I tried entering proxy details directly in DBeaver and connecting through Multi Agent installed on my computer. All three methods returned the same five orders."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The versions used were QueryPie ACP Community 11.6.7 and MySQL 8.0.42. All customers and orders shown below are fictional lab data."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. Connecting a Database and Querying It"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "First, I started another MySQL container, separate from QueryPie’s internal database."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I named the database orders_demo and inserted four customers into customers and 12 orders into orders. Looking up pending orders and counting by status would be sufficient to test connectivity and querying."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In MySQL, I created orders_reader with SELECT permission only on orders_demo. As this exercise only involves queries, the database account gets only that privilege. This is separate from the QueryPie user privileges configured later."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "With preparation complete, I registered the database as an administrator and then connected as a developer."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. Registering MySQL in QueryPie"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "After signing in as an administrator, I created a MySQL connection under Databases → Connection Management → DB Connections with the following values."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "bulletList",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Connection name: Orders Demo MySQL"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Database type: MySQL"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Host / Port: orders-db / 3306"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Database Name: orders_demo"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Database account: orders_reader"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "For Host, I used orders-db rather than localhost. QueryPie and MySQL share a Docker network, so the container name is reachable. Here, localhost would refer to the QueryPie container itself."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This should be checked first when connecting a company database too. What matters is whether the QueryPie server can reach it, rather than whether my own PC can."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/first-database-connection/01.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 1. Test Connection returned a successful connection message.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 1. Test Connection returned a successful connection message."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I entered the database account and password, clicked Test Connection, confirmed success, and saved."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I also checked Hide this credential from Connection List page to hide the source database credentials from users’ connection lists. I would check how the password appeared after signing in as the developer."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/first-database-connection/02.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 2. Orders Demo MySQL is registered. Next comes the developer account.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 2. Orders Demo MySQL is registered. Next comes the developer account."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. Giving the Developer Read-Only Access"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Testing only as an administrator can miss what developers actually see. Under General → User Management → Users, I created Demo Developer with login ID demo-dev and administrator role None."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/first-database-connection/03.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 3. Developer account demo-dev added below the existing qp-admin administrator.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 3. Developer account demo-dev added below the existing qp-admin administrator."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I then opened Databases → DB Access Control → Access Control, selected Demo Developer, and used Grant Privilege to grant Read-Only access to Orders Demo MySQL."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/first-database-connection/04.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 4. demo-dev granted Read-Only access to Orders Demo MySQL.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 4. demo-dev granted Read-Only access to Orders Demo MySQL."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Registering a database and granting users access were separate steps. I granted a single user directly here; team groups would likely be easier at scale. Expiration dates are also worth considering for temporary access."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "4. Signing In as the Developer and Querying Orders"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I signed in as demo-dev and changed the password as required at first login. Expanding QueryPie Connections under Databases displayed Orders Demo MySQL."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Selecting it showed Read-Only (User), Select permission, and Active status. The developer had not needed to enter the original MySQL password."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/first-database-connection/05.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 5. Checking the database and privileges in the developer view, then clicking Connect.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 5. Checking the database and privileges in the developer view, then clicking Connect."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Connect opened the web SQL editor. I queried pending orders in orders_demo."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "codeBlock",
      "attrs": {
        "language": null
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "SELECT order_id, customer_id, order_date, status, total_amount\nFROM orders\nWHERE status = 'PENDING'\nORDER BY order_date, order_id\nLIMIT 20;"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/first-database-connection/06.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 6. Five pending orders: 1001, 1003, 1006, 1009, and 1012.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 6. Five pending orders: 1001, 1003, 1006, 1009, and 1012."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "After confirming the list, I counted orders by status."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "codeBlock",
      "attrs": {
        "language": null
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "SELECT status, COUNT(*) AS order_count\nFROM orders\nGROUP BY status\nORDER BY status;"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/first-database-connection/07.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 7. CANCELLED: 2, DELIVERED: 3, PENDING: 5, SHIPPED: 2—12 in total, matching the inserted data.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 7. CANCELLED: 2, DELIVERED: 3, PENDING: 5, SHIPPED: 2—12 in total, matching the inserted data."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "From the developer’s perspective, the steps were simply signing in to QueryPie, choosing a database, and running SQL. No separate MySQL account or password had to be shared."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Queries alone do not cover all work. Copying or exporting results and transaction-related permissions were unchecked for this account. A real team would need to enable and test the capabilities it requires."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "5. Connecting with DBeaver Too"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Next, I queried the same orders in DBeaver. Connecting through the QueryPie proxy allows SQL execution from an existing database client."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I used Agentless Proxy: the database client connects to QueryPie’s proxy without installing a separate agent."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Back in the administrator view, I enabled Proxy Usage in the database connection details, selected Use QueryPie registered account, and saved. QueryPie then connects to MySQL using the previously registered database account."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/first-database-connection/08.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 8. Proxy Usage enabled with the registered database account. Query Audit is also On.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 8. Proxy Usage enabled with the registered database account. Query Audit is also On."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In the developer view, Proxy Info showed port 40000. I clicked Create Token to obtain a Username and Password for the connection. DBeaver uses this token instead of the original MySQL password."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The token is visible only when issued, so I stored it securely. If lost, it must be revoked and reissued. The capture below shows guidance without the token value."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/first-database-connection/09.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 9. Proxy Info shows the connection port and token creation menu.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 9. Proxy Info shows the connection port and token creation menu."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I opened DBeaver and created a new MySQL connection."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "bulletList",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Host: 127.0.0.1"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Port: 40000"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Database: orders_demo"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Username / Password: proxy token issued by the developer account"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I used 127.0.0.1 because QueryPie and DBeaver run on the same Mac. For multiple employees, use a QueryPie proxy address reachable from their PCs and check that the firewall permits its port."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Test Connection reported MySQL 8.0.42. I then pasted the same pending-orders query used in the web editor."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/first-database-connection/10.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 10. DBeaver returned the same five orders as the web editor.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 10. DBeaver returned the same five orders as the web editor."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The SQL was identical in the browser and DBeaver. In DBeaver, only the address, port, and login details were configured for the QueryPie proxy. At least for this MySQL query, I could keep my existing database tool."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "6. Connecting Through Multi Agent on My Computer"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Besides entering connection details manually, an agent can be installed on the computer. I installed QueryPie Multi Agent and opened DBeaver from its database list."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "From the top-right QueryPie profile menu, I selected Download & Support → Multi-Agent. Installers for Mac, Windows, and Linux were available; I downloaded Apple Silicon for my Mac. The server provided agent version v9."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/first-database-connection/11.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 11. Downloading the installer for the OS and copying the QueryPie address shown below.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 11. Downloading the installer for the OS and copying the QueryPie address shown below."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I opened the downloaded DMG and copied QueryPieMultiAgent into Applications."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/first-database-connection/12.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 12. Mac installation: copy the app to Applications, then launch it.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 12. Mac installation: copy the app to Applications, then launch it."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The agent needs the QueryPie web address, not the database address. I registered http://localhost:8000. If another host is already registered, Settings → Add New Host adds one. Multiple QueryPie hosts can be registered—hence Multi Agent."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/first-database-connection/13.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 13. Entering the lab server address in QueryPie Host.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 13. Entering the lab server address in QueryPie Host."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Selecting the server opened a login form. I signed in with demo-dev, the same developer account used on the web."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/first-database-connection/14.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 14. The agent also uses the developer’s own QueryPie account.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 14. The agent also uses the developer’s own QueryPie account."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "An administrator must first register the proxy address agents will use. Since QueryPie and the agent run on the same Mac, I registered 127.0.0.1 following the official initial-configuration guide. A company server needs an IP or domain reachable from employee PCs. This is administrator setup, not something each developer configures in a database."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Expanding QueryPie Connections under Databases showed Orders Demo MySQL, with orders-db and Read-Only (User) below it. The agent reflected the privileges granted in the web interface."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/first-database-connection/15.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 15. The agent lists the database and read permissions granted to the developer.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 15. The agent lists the database and read permissions granted to the developer."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I right-clicked orders-db and selected Open Connection With → DBeaver. A connection named Orders Demo MySQL was added to DBeaver. There was no need to issue a web token and enter each connection setting manually."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/first-database-connection/16.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 16. Opening DBeaver directly from the database list.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 16. Opening DBeaver directly from the database list."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I opened the added connection and ran the same pending-orders query in a new SQL editor. Orders 1001, 1003, 1006, 1009, and 1012 appeared again."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/first-database-connection/17.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 17. Results from the Multi Agent-created connection match the same five orders.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 17. Results from the Multi Agent-created connection match the same five orders."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The difference was in preparing the connection. Without the agent, I entered the token and settings manually. With Multi Agent, I signed in, selected a database, and opened DBeaver. Teams connecting to many databases daily may want to compare both approaches."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "7. What Still Needs Checking Before Company Use"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Connecting it myself made the adoption discussions—and who needs to be involved—more concrete."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "First, decide who registers databases and grants privileges. I played both roles here; a company needs a defined approver for developer requests. The same applies to revoking privileges after transfers or departures."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Test the tools the team actually uses. I ran simple SELECTs with MySQL and DBeaver; DataGrip or other databases need their own tests. I have not yet checked large query volumes or transactions."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Security features cannot be verified from settings alone. Does Read-Only actually block modifications? What happens to an existing session after revocation? Query Audit was On, but I will inspect how users and SQL are logged in the next article."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "8. Checking Direct Database Access Paths Too"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This brought me back to Part 1’s idea of control after intrusion. Access through QueryPie worked. But what if a direct route to the original database remains?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "That route remains in my lab. For comparison and checks, MySQL is directly reachable on the Mac at 127.0.0.1:13306. The QueryPie proxy port used in DBeaver is 40000."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A company rollout should address this too: restrict allowed connection sources and check who holds the original database credentials. Hiding credentials in the connection list does not block direct access by itself."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "To keep access under QueryPie’s control even if database passwords or a developer PC are compromised, these connection paths need attention too."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Next: Trying Modification Queries"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I registered the database, signed in as a developer, and queried orders from the web editor and DBeaver. In DBeaver, I tried both manual connection details and Multi Agent. Users could run SQL in a familiar tool while accessing the database with privileges granted in QueryPie."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Part 4 will go further: what message appears when a read-only account attempts a change, what happens after revocation, and where the records remain. Since the source database account also has only SELECT, I will distinguish which layer blocks the operation."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "References: "
        },
